WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:02.740
- So, you meet somebody, you meet a girl

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.081
and you're interested in her, like,

00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:05.015
so what do you do?

00:00:05.015 --> 00:00:06.276
Well, I tend bar over at blah, blah, blah.

00:00:06.276 --> 00:00:07.577
They're like, oh, so
what do you really do?

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:10.503
And I'm like, no, I really
do that, in fact I was there

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:14.003
just a couple hours ago, I really do that.

00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:18.229
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.229 --> 00:00:19.897
Over the last 25 years I've spent

00:00:19.897 --> 00:00:21.648
the vast majority of that working

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:23.235
the front of house restaurants,

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:24.859
both bar tending and serving, managing.

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:27.539
Yeah, server and bar
tender has been in my blood

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:29.049
for two decades.

00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:31.205
I've done fine dining and
I've worked in wine bars

00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:32.588
and I've done breakfast joints.

00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:33.968
God, breakfast joints are so much fun.

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:35.645
It gets in you and it's an addiction.

00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:37.678
A few years back I was
dating a girl at the time

00:00:37.678 --> 00:00:39.873
that was encouraging me, she
was working in corporate,

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.691
was very successful, so I
pursued having a normal job,

00:00:43.691 --> 00:00:45.523
that's when I had my
desk job, my normal job.

00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:47.272
And I ended up working in insurance.

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:49.344
I went through the training
and I went through all this,

00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:51.378
I was getting up every
morning and havin' my coffee,

00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:54.550
driving into work, I
would sit in this cubicle,

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.383
that's really what people wanna do,

00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:58.183
and it's like, I can't
judge anybody for it,

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.262
but for me I just
remember that one morning,

00:01:00.262 --> 00:01:02.295
like, it just hit me and I just sat down

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.635
and I just started crying.

00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:06.516
I went from tending bar
to having a desk job

00:01:06.516 --> 00:01:08.592
and I went from working four days a week

00:01:08.592 --> 00:01:11.842
to working five days a week
and I took a third pay cut.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:13.629
I guess I kinda convinced myself

00:01:13.629 --> 00:01:16.191
having a more adult job was the next thing

00:01:16.191 --> 00:01:17.570
I had to be doing.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.621
Once I let go of that, and I
started working weekend brunch

00:01:20.621 --> 00:01:22.982
at a little joint in my
neighborhood I'm like,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.160
I was workin' seven days a week,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.218
people were like, aren't you nuts,

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.358
you're working seven days a week,

00:01:26.358 --> 00:01:27.537
and I'm like, no, no, no,
I'm at work five days a week

00:01:27.537 --> 00:01:29.405
and I get to go have fun at a restaurant

00:01:29.405 --> 00:01:30.505
on the weekends.

00:01:30.505 --> 00:01:32.742
'Cause like that, oh, my
God, I was moving again,

00:01:32.742 --> 00:01:34.812
I felt energized, I was so like,

00:01:34.812 --> 00:01:36.802
it was amazing how much
it was giving back to me.

00:01:36.802 --> 00:01:39.122
When you're in the bar
and restaurant business

00:01:39.122 --> 00:01:40.505
you meet some of the
most fascinating people

00:01:40.505 --> 00:01:41.685
from all walks of life.

00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:43.108
I mean, people who have
traveled the world,

00:01:43.108 --> 00:01:46.319
ministers, acupuncturists, master masons.

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:49.977
People I would never have
ever come into contact with

00:01:49.977 --> 00:01:52.050
if I didn't work behind the bar

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.555
or on the floor of a restaurant.

00:01:53.555 --> 00:01:55.877
I work four days a week
and I have three days

00:01:55.877 --> 00:01:58.073
that I don't have to be anywhere

00:01:58.073 --> 00:01:59.499
unless I've scheduled some things.

00:01:59.499 --> 00:02:01.204
For me it's really important to have

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:02.993
down time where I get
to work on side projects

00:02:02.993 --> 00:02:04.823
and I get to have time to travel.

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:06.087
Right before I came to do this

00:02:06.087 --> 00:02:07.633
I had a meeting with a guy about

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:09.626
a business model for a new concept.

00:02:09.626 --> 00:02:12.310
At home I'm working on
three woodworking projects.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:16.173
I used to write for a magazine,
host beer tasting classes.

00:02:16.173 --> 00:02:18.327
I know that my lifestyle's
not the most traditional,

00:02:18.327 --> 00:02:21.077
but it's the way I need it to be.

00:02:23.655 --> 00:02:25.446
Sincerely, you just quit giving

00:02:25.446 --> 00:02:28.421
so much of a fuck about
what other people think.

00:02:28.421 --> 00:02:30.671
(laughter)

00:02:36.427 --> 00:02:38.677
(cheering)

